    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting **1 July**, labelled by the calendar year it starts in \u2014 e.g. a registration on 2026\u201109\u201106 \u2192 **FY26**).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec):\n   - Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema.\n   - Updated the `membershipNumber` doc: its year segment now uses the fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n   - Updated the `membershipPoints` doc: the +3 bonus now fires when tenure exceeds one fiscal year rather than 365 days.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n   - Added `fiscalYearNumber(LocalDate)` \u2014 the July-start fiscal-year calendar year (`month \u2265 July ? year : year-1`).\n   - Added `fiscalYear(Owner)` returning `FY<YY>`, and wired the `fiscalYear` mapping.\n   - `membershipNumber` now derives `M<YY>` from the fiscal year instead of the raw registration year.\n   - Replaced `tenureDays` (365-day windows) with `tenureFiscalYears` (elapsed fiscal years = FY(now) \u2212 FY(registration)); `membershipPoints` now adds 3 when that count is `> 1`.\n\nThe stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted in the controller, so all fiscal-year derivations correctly key off the adjusted date. The new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n**One design decision worth flagging:** the spec says `FY<YY>` but doesn't state whether the label is the fiscal year's *start* or *end* calendar year. I chose the **start-year** convention because the existing `membershipNumber` example (`M26`) stays consistent with a registration around today's date (Sept 2026). If your intended convention is the end year (Australian \"FY26 = year ending 30 June 2026\"), it's a one-line change in `fiscalYearNumber` \u2014 let me know and I'll flip it.",
